ulture and Conflict Navigation", "description": "Stage managers often notice tension before anyone else does. This section teaches students to build trust, communicate across difference, and respond to conflict with clarity, humility, and appropriate escalation.", "children": [{"id": "fba7d4cc-842f-4df7-be7e-299db890bbe3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inclusive rehearsal practice", "children": [{"id": "e7e22c6e-ca9b-4a17-a961-91881e800a07", "type": "concept", "title": "Name and pronoun practices"}, {"id": "2aa4d636-d00e-420e-bd0c-e7ffc7bf0789", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural humility"}, {"id": "06c92db8-266a-4eb9-8ed5-169c61295073", "type": "concept", "title": "Religious and caregiving needs"}, {"id": "e8a54285-46b5-4684-a456-185d29479362", "type": "concept", "title": "Transparent expectations"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students learn habits that make rooms more equitable and easier to participate in."}, {"id": "9d75bd9c-0598-4901-88b3-fe2db649e2d2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Conflict navigation", "children": [{"id": "54433c68-cb2e-4f8b-8691-1be11077c102", "type": "concept", "title": "Listening"}, {"id": "af2ef318-a852-4cee-80d4-e77c2081e595", "type": "concept", "title": "Documentation"}, {"id": "a9748f9b-de4c-47ea-af8e-4b84a16b2515", "type": "concept", "title": "Mediation boundaries"}, {"id": "09e33893-51d3-40ed-beb2-d4636bcd4999", "type": "concept", "title": "Escalation"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students practice separating facts, impacts, needs, and decisions when conflict appears."}, {"id": "58e33db1-c380-4c75-be61-11614643778c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Power and accountability", "children": [{"id": "599ee44f-755e-4155-ae0f-c9e8e16fc6fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Mandated reporting"}, {"id": "32b1b9cd-3666-4407-9562-fb11fb92e267", "type": "concept", "title": "Harassment concerns"}, {"id": "ed9c6712-1ca5-4878-9031-e8a7b0ee5fc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Confidentiality limits"}, {"id": "c5e8d37a-105c-4f4a-a96e-82c7922520ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Retaliation awareness"}], "description": "Why learn it: The focus is recognizing when the stage manager can solve a problem and when the issue belongs to leadership, HR, faculty, or union channels."}]}, {"id": "ab515051-fb5a-4783-b594-8ace6a174b62", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone Simulation and Portfolio", "description": "The course culminates in applied stage management scenarios and a professional portfolio. Students demonstrate that they can synthesize communication, paperwork, cueing, safety, collaboration, and leadership under realistic conditions.", "children": [{"id": "34fa6942-c7d2-42e4-951b-1b8edbbe0722", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Simulation lab", "children": [{"id": "da449868-a0b2-495b-8bd0-cce02278a9f6", "type": "concept", "title": "Late actor"}, {"id": "38a9f939-6361-4ee4-82bd-add75dcaa53a", "type": "concept", "title": "Cue change"}, {"id": "5115d876-5a89-4b30-b1ec-7e08af17c87d", "type": "concept", "title": "Prop failure"}, {"id": "526f27f7-4c6e-41bf-bbdc-2ea88173d2f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Schedule compression"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students respond to rehearsal, tech, and performance scenarios that require prioritization and judgment."}, {"id": "3e2de01a-85da-4059-b5e4-df85e565ac09", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Portfolio assembly", "children": [{"id": "294fa81f-c4c5-4a91-993b-e66edf113272", "type": "concept", "title": "Prompt book excerpt"}, {"id": "f76468dc-c9a2-4f2f-b595-a8185e99c7b4", "type": "concept", "title": "Reports"}, {"id": "93d75e8b-6e1d-40cb-b1e2-314cd6ac2203", "type": "concept", "title": "Run sheet"}, {"id": "a1101711-361b-46da-b9dc-4ffb9db57c92", "type": "concept", "title": "Cue page"}], "description": "Why learn it: Students curate polished samples that show their process and readiness for internships or production assignments."}, {"id": "d8d00274-5fe2-48e0-b2c4-9d9f0d5179e6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reflective practice", "children": [{"id": "5daf847b-22ac-4fc4-9f69-7812